  "description": "Hosts ordinary Windows Forms forms as real MDI children of an MDI frame the .NET code does not own - a legacy VB6 or ActiveX host, or a frame on another thread. Creates a native WS_EX_MDICHILD window, reparents the form into it, and keeps captions, icons, sizing, activation, maximized state and MDI keyboard accelerators in step. Registrable for COM interop as an ActiveX control.",
